  "id": "Compound::DB00786 - Gene::10893",
  "verbalization": "Marimastat is likely to interact with Mmp24 through a shared pathway involving matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs). The evidence suggests that Marimastat binds to Mmp23b, Mmp27, and Mmp26, all of which are part of the MMP family and are participated in by Mmp24. This indicates that Marimastat may influence Mmp24 through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of MMPs. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent interaction, though the specific molecular mechanism remains unclear. The presence of multiple MMPs in the pathway implies that Marimastat may act as a regulator of MMP activity, potentially through binding to these proteins and affecting their function. This relationship is supported by the observed participation of Mmp24 in the MMP pathway, suggesting a possible dependency on MMP activity for Marimastat's effects.",
